Patch summary:
Report the Vulkan image's row pitch from stream_renderer_resource_get_info.
The VMM exports a ColorBuffer's memory as a dma-buf when the guest scans it
out, and describes it to the display with this stride. The packed width * bpp
is wrong for the padded or tiled layouts the driver picks (RADV aligns pitches
to its swizzle block), so ask vkGetImageSubresourceLayout when the ColorBuffer
has a Vulkan image and report that pitch instead.
